00:05:11.025 --> 00:05:13.035
So I want to talk about inflation.

00:05:13.185 --> 00:05:16.335
So tomorrow I have another
session with Sahra and we're

00:05:16.335 --> 00:05:17.565
going to talk about inflation.

00:05:17.715 --> 00:05:22.365
And again, she will create a report
and send it to me with the recording.

00:05:22.875 --> 00:05:29.625
So I'm hoping to get, getting back to
my discussion of the, uh, hockey stick.

00:05:29.925 --> 00:05:33.855
I've sort of progressed past that
steep blade of the hockey stick

00:05:33.895 --> 00:05:36.810
stage and I'm somewhere here.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:42.620
I'm not sure where I am, but I'm at the
beginning of that long road from B1 to B2.

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:45.360
I consider that to be the longest stretch.

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:49.770
Some people say no, the longest
stretch is from B2 to C1.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:54.510
Uh, I mean, it's kind of arbitrary
because unless you actually take a

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:59.010
test and I don't take a test, but I
consider B2 means I'm comfortable.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:05:59.730
I make mistakes.

00:05:59.730 --> 00:06:01.020
I understand most things.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.200
Uh, C1 means I make far fewer misses.

00:06:04.935 --> 00:06:09.344
And there's nothing that I don't
understand, but I'm not quite at the

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:13.125
level of vocabulary of a native or C2.

00:06:13.125 --> 00:06:16.155
